<title>JAPAN: Mexico, Petronas to launch samurai bonds--sources.</title>
<headline>Mexico, Petronas to launch samurai bonds--sources.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico and Malaysia&quot;s state-owned Petroliam Nasional (Petronas) may launch samurai bonds, possibly as early as this week, underwriting sources in Tokyo said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Mexico is considering the launch of about 50 billion yen worth of samurais, with a maturity of seven years.</p>
<p>&quot;If the market condition allows, Mexico may launch samurais as soon as this week,&quot; one underwriting source said.</p>
<p>Separately, Petronas is also planning to launch a total of about 30 billion yen worth of samurais.</p>
<p>Underwriters said that they are likely to be divided into two to three tranches, with a maturity of 16 years.</p>
<p>One of the four major Japanese brokerage houses is expected to lead-manage both Mexico&quot;s and Petronas&quot; samurai issues.</p>
</text>
